WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.860
Hey guys, it’s Jan here.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.660
I cannot wait for Season 5 of Game Of Thrones
to kick off.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.390
So, while we’re all gearing up to the new
season, I’m going to be taking a look at

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.760
some of the show’s highlights so far.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:17.150
This video is all about Tywin Lannister’s
top 10 moments.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:22.860
A no-nonsense man with an authoritative demeanour,
Tywin’s insistence on family and legacy

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:27.200
above all else made him the Godfather of the
Game of Thrones world.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.350
His cruel and calculating nature was even
immortalised in song.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:35.730
Remember The Rains of Castamere, which commemorated
the time Tywin brutally killed all of House

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.309
Reyne when they rebelled against his father
Tytos?

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:41.179
He truly was the Tywin-ator!

00:00:41.179 --> 00:00:45.110
And Charles Dance played him to perfection,
turning the ruthless and politically savvy

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:48.329
Tywin into one of our favourite characters
on the show.

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:52.500
So, let’s countdown Tywin’s top 10 moments!

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:58.089
As the judges took a break from Tyrion’s
trial, Jaime offered his father a deal: in

00:00:58.089 --> 00:01:02.019
exchange for his brother’s life, he’d
do what he’d previously refused to do.

00:01:02.019 --> 00:01:06.770
He’d leave the Kingsguard, go to Casterly
Rock, marry a suitable woman and carry on

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.570
the Lannister line.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:14.689
Tywin agreed without so much as batting an
eye, leaving Jaime looking more than a little

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:15.689
shocked.

00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:19.310
Oh, Jaime, you walked right into that one,
mate!

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:20.310
Doh!

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:25.299
Good job for Jaime that Tywin’s not around
anymore to make him keep his word!

00:01:25.299 --> 00:01:30.500
Tyrion visited his father to ask for Casterly
Rock, which he believed he was entitled to

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.179
as lawful heir, given that Kingsguard Jaime
couldn’t inherit.

00:01:34.179 --> 00:01:39.149
Tywin, however, saw things rather differently
and told Tyrion he’d rather be consumed

00:01:39.149 --> 00:01:45.840
by maggots than make him heir to the family
stronghold as he regarded Tyrion as an “ill-made,

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.499
spiteful little creature full of envy, lust,
and low cunning.”

00:01:49.499 --> 00:01:54.850
In this scene, we really saw Tywin’s cruelty
and coldness to his son Tyrion, who he not

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:59.179
only blamed for the death of his wife Joanna
but also accused of sullying the Lannister

00:01:59.179 --> 00:02:01.539
name by consorting with prostitutes.

00:02:01.539 --> 00:02:06.100
He even threatened to hang the next one he
found in Tyrion’s bed.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:14.070
Which is hypocritical given that Tyrion later
found his former lover Shae in Tywin’s bed.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:18.920
We always knew that Tywin was a master of
the game, but apparently he was also a frustrated

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:19.920
school teacher.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:25.230
I mean, did you see him teaching Tommen about
kingly qualities as they stood right next

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.490
to Joffrey’s corpse?

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:30.730
Tywin was loving it; Cersei, however, was
most definitely not.

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:35.870
Then there was Tywin’s classic line to Tommen,
“Your brother was not a wise king; your

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:40.780
brother was not a good king; if he had been,
perhaps he’d still be alive.”

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:44.910
He even started giving Tommen a lesson about
the birds and the bees!

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:49.130
Can you just imagine being taught that by
Tywin Lannister?!

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:55.930
Olenna may be a master of political power
games, just like Tywin, but when the Tyrell

00:02:55.930 --> 00:03:02.090
matriarch and the Lannister patriarch went
toe to toe in season 3, it was Tywin who came

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:04.760
out on top, at least at the time.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:10.150
It was just fantastic to watch their pretty
evenly-matched verbal sparring session as

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:14.740
Olenna refused to marry her grandson Loras
to Tywin’s daughter Cersei.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:20.290
Little did she know that Tywin was well aware
of her plans to marry Loras to Sansa Stark!

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:25.790
The pair traded jibes, yet nothing would change
Olenna’s mind until Tywin played his trump

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:30.201
card, pulling out his quill and threatening
to make Loras part of the Kingsguard, which

00:03:30.201 --> 00:03:33.950
would have meant no heirs or Highgarden for
him.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:39.230
As Olenna caved, what a wonderful line she
delivered to Tywin: “it’s a rare enough

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:43.620
thing, a man who lives up to his reputation”.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:48.870
In a brilliant bit of deviation from the books,
Tywin rode into Harrenhal like a boss, stopped

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:52.520
the prisoners being tortured by his men, and
chose Arya as his cupbearer.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:58.060
Though Arya was disguised as a boy, Tywin,
immediately recognised her as a smart young

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.060
girl.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:03.460
Their scenes together were great to watch
as they showed a slightly warmer side to Tywin

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.910
than usual, as he grew to sort of respect
Arya.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:12.300
The best moment came when talk turned to Aegon
Targaryen who Tywin said attacked Harrenhal

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:16.910
with his dragons; but Arya corrected him,
adding that Aegon’s sisters Rhaenys and

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:20.250
Visenya were also responsible for the Targaryen
triumph.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:25.650
This was the moment we saw Tywin let Arya
know that he knew she wasn’t really who

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:27.090
she claimed to be.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:32.360
In the end, Tywin seemed to let her off the
hook, but it was certainly a dangerous moment.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:36.220
To see what Charles Dance and Maisie Williams
said about shooting these scenes, check out

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:39.130
my interviews with them here.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:44.260
The Lannisters were so famed for their wealth
that people joked Tywin Lannister even shitted

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:45.260
gold.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:49.350
So, it was fitting he should end his days
sat on a toilet while Tyrion confronted him

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.350
with a crossbow.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:55.580
And I couldn’t help but think how doubly
appropriate it was that Tywin got that crossbow

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:59.460
in his gut given how we first met him gutting
a stag.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:02.460
The gutter became the guttee, so to speak.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:07.260
Adding to the aptness of Papa Lannister’s
last scene was the fact it aired on Father’s

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:08.260
Day.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:12.860
Yes, the parting gift Tyrion gave his father
before fleeing King’s Landing certainly

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:13.940
seemed well deserved.

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:19.610
After all, Tyrion had just discovered his
former lover Shae in Tywin’s bed and Tywin

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:24.160
did dismiss her as nothing more than a whore
after Tyrion revealed his love for her.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:30.270
Oh yes, and there was that small matter of
Tywin having always wanted Tyrion dead.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:33.590
In the end, though, it was Tyrion who was
the death of Tywin.

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:39.440
And as Papa Lannister shuffled off this mortal
coil, I remembered his words in season 3 to

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:45.930
Olenna Tyrell that his “stomach remained
quite strong”… yeah, just not quite strong

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:49.900
enough to withstand a crossbow, hey, Tywin?!

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:54.160
When Joffrey summoned Tywin to the Throne
Room to get a report on the Small Council,

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:58.200
let’s just say it didn’t exactly go the
way the King was hoping.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:02.880
Instead of filling Joffrey in on the details,
Tywin told his grandson he was welcome to

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.220
attend the meetings himself!

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:10.150
I love the way Tywin still managed to talk
down to Joffrey even though he was standing

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:15.970
at the bottom of the steps to the Iron Throne,
and Joffrey was above him, sitting on the

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:16.970
Throne.

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:20.930
But the scene got even better when Joffrey
complained about Tywin moving the council

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:26.320
meetings to the Tower of the Hand, which meant
the boy-King would have to actually walk up

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:27.510
some steps!

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:31.970
Clearly, Joffrey had forgotten just who he
was dealing with at this point – I mean,

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:36.790
Tywin was one of the few people who wouldn’t
put up with the King’s crap, after all.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:42.990
And just when you thought Tywin was intimidating
enough standing below Joffrey, he strode up

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:48.180
those steps to the throne and towered over
him, adding, “We could arrange to have you

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.790
carried there.”

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:55.510
And what about that smirk on Tywin’s face
as he walked away from the King?!

00:06:55.510 --> 00:07:01.300
The very first time we saw Tywin on screen,
he acted like a total boss, as you’d expect,

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:06.900
While he gutted and skinned a stag with ruthless
efficiency, he lectured his son Jaime on the

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:11.150
importance of family legacy and what it really
took to be a Lannister.

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:16.010
And what about those great Lannister lines
that Charles Dance delivered, including “A

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:20.960
lion doesn’t concern himself with the opinions
of the sheep”, as he told Jaime not to worry

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:23.650
about what other people thought of him.

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:28.240
And when he gave Jaime half the Lannister
forces, he ominously told his son to remind

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.980
Catelyn Stark that “Lannisters pay their
debts”.

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.250
This was an incredible scene where we really
learned why Tywin would do anything to ensure

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.250
the Lannisters’ survival.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:36.180
Oh, and of course, that stag he butchered
was a nice metaphor for the fate of House

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:37.730
Baratheon.

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:43.610
Tywin’s late arrival with an army of Lannister
and Tyrell soldiers at the Battle of Blackwater

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:44.760
may have saved the day.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:51.590
But, could anyone other than Tywin Lannister
actually get away with riding his horse into

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:54.900
the King’s Throne Room without so much as
a please or thank-you?

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:59.360
Hell, he even let his horse shit on the threshold
to the room!

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:04.180
Still, knowing Tywin, I guess Joffrey and
Cersei would have just been grateful that

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:09.580
he didn’t leave a steaming pile of manure
right in front of the Iron Throne!

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:14.730
And did he get down off his steed when accepting
the titles “Saviour of the City” and “Hand

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.610
of the King” from his grandson Joffrey?

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:19.330
Are you out of your mind?!

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:22.490
This is Tywin Lannister we’re talking about!

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:28.949
Tywin didn’t shy away from putting anyone
in their place, so, when Joffrey started an

00:08:28.949 --> 00:08:34.469
argument with Tyrion at a small council meeting,
threatening his uncle and vowing to serve

00:08:34.469 --> 00:08:38.639
Robb Stark’s head to Sansa, Tywin put his
foot firmly down.

00:08:38.639 --> 00:08:45.550
As an enraged Joffrey screamed “I am the
king”, Tywin interjected: “Any man who

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:48.709
must say ‘I am the king’ is no true king.

00:08:48.709 --> 00:08:53.070
I’ll make sure you understand that when
I’ve won your war for you.”

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:59.990
Then, with his trademark glare, Tywin stared
down Joffrey as the boy-King accused his grandfather

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:05.230
of hiding under Casterly Rock while Joffrey’s
father won the real war!

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:09.040
Oh, Joffrey, you really overstepped the mark
there!

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:14.579
And by the look on your face, you realised
it, just a little bit too late!

00:09:14.579 --> 00:09:21.889
And who can forget Tywin’s fabulous, ice-cold
reply: “The king is tired, see him to his

00:09:21.889 --> 00:09:27.459
chambers”; which he finished off with a
final verbal slap-down, ordering Pycelle to

00:09:27.459 --> 00:09:31.120
give Joffrey some essence of Nightshade to
help him sleep.

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:37.949
What a fantastic scene and who didn’t cheer
as Tywin treated Joffrey like the spoiled,

00:09:37.949 --> 00:09:39.910
little brat he really was?!

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:44.850
In fact, there were so many great Tywin moments
over the seasons that I’ve got to give an

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.420
honourable mention to one moment that didn’t
quite make my top 10:

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:52.379
When Tyrion went to tell his father he’d
succeeded in getting the Tyrells to cough

00:09:52.379 --> 00:09:57.920
up some cash for the royal wedding, he wasn’t
expecting to leave the meeting with an order

00:09:57.920 --> 00:09:59.480
to marry Sansa Stark.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:04.059
But that’s exactly what happened, as Tywin
told him he wasn’t about to let the Tyrells

00:10:04.059 --> 00:10:08.220
steal the key to the north by marrying Loras
to the eldest Stark daughter.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:14.139
As Cersei sat there, all smug at having stitched
up her younger brother – remember it was

00:10:14.139 --> 00:10:19.040
her who told Tywin about the Tyrell plot – little
did she know that she was next in the line

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.600
of marital fire.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:26.910
And her protests did no good as Tywin stated
stonily that she had to marry Loras, breed

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:29.910
and end the rumours about her once and for
all.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:32.769
So what are your favourite Tywin moments?

00:10:32.769 --> 00:10:34.559
How much are you going to miss him in the
show?

00:10:34.559 --> 00:10:38.170
Let me know in the comments below.

